_RESEARCH","owner":"sfkunal","html_url":"https://github.com/sfkunal/DataPrivacy_RESEARCH","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"The world of technology is changing. It used to be one where users could post on social media, order clothes online, and play mobile games without a care in the world. As time progressed, companies eventually realized that they could collect small pieces of information from a user\u2019s technological habits, and use that to form a profile of the user of some sort. I used a packet-monitoring service to listen in on third-party applications and wrote a script to filter out relevant pieces of data that were being sent back to an application\u2019s server. The findings of this study concluded that third-party iOS applications have unmonitored power to access pieces of information like contacts, location, and emails.","topics":[],"score":177391,"global_rank":440810},{"name":"addyg/NewsWebsiteCrawler","owner":"addyg","html_url":"https://github.com/addyg/NewsWebsiteCrawler","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Crawl news websites with Crawler4j","topics":[],"score":177391,"global_rank":440811},{"name":"erinsteiner-NOAA/fisheryconfidentiality","owner":"erinsteiner-NOAA","html_url":"https://github.com/erinsteiner-NOAA/fisheryconfidentiality","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Fledgling project to build tools to work with confidential fisheries data","topics":[],"score":177391,"global_rank":440812},{"name":"Seon2020/reading-notes","owner":"Seon2020","html_url":"https://github.com/Seon2020/reading-notes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Code Fellows Reading Notes","topics":[],"score":177391,"global_rank":440813},{"name":"Coltonchristensen-charliepup/code-201-reading-notes","owner":"Coltonchristensen-charliepup","html_url":"https://github.com/Coltonchristensen-charliepup/code-201-readi